Z||000000||Cozmo||11-02-2001||09:10 AM||||OK dumb me I tore one of the outer CV joints on my '86 GT when removing the cradle.<BR>It looks like a real PITA to put a new one on. Is there an easy way?<BR>Has anyone used those "EZ-boots"; the ones with the zipper?<P>Thanks,<BR>BobC||||reg||5
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||11-02-2001||09:59 AM||||I've used split boots on the outer joints with great success. Care must be taken however when installing it. Read directions CAREFULLY, it's easy to screw one up.<BR>Only other alternative is to replace with a new one piece boot or a remanufactured axle.<BR>Cost run around $50.00 here.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Lisa 86 2m4||11-04-2001||04:19 PM||||I guess I should have been there to supervise! But don't be too hard on yourself, it's just another opportunity to learn how to do one more new thing!!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cozmo||11-04-2001||08:10 PM||||Thanks, Indy...<BR>It looks like those E-Z boots will work if I take my time and follow the instructions.<BR>Lisa... did you get the Mr. Mikes seats in yet??? <BR>Yeah, I could use some supervision around here <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>BobC<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||jeffndebrus||11-04-2001||08:11 PM||||ohhh baby!||||reg||10
Z||000005||Lisa 86 2m4||11-04-2001||09:39 PM||||Got one in. Hoping to do the other next weekend. Just no motivation! Must be the time change. But let me tell you, it looks so nice!! Let me know if you need supervision on any of your projects!!||||reg||10
Z||000006||Fie Ro||11-05-2001||07:48 AM||||I replaced one with a one-piece boot and it wasn't hard to do. A mechanic once did one on my former GT and I remembered how he did it ;-)) Remove the wheel, disconnect the rear (lower) balljoint and the toe-link, loosen (do not remove) the 3 nuts on top of the struttower. with some twisting you'll get the axle out.<BR>My boot was torn by a rubbing handbrake cable (which was bad reinstalled by a fiero "specialist" shop!) Found that out when the second boot failed within a week :-(||||reg||12
Z||000007||FieroPerformance||11-05-2001||04:27 PM||||I would remove the inside one and slide a new boot down the rear axel.||||reg||1
